-- the entry as code that names its three parts, and the schedule that holds them: a definition's own
-- code is the quote of its value, in which every part is already unfolded and a stuck part copied at
-- each use (nk-demo-m's weighs 1,493,231 nodes; nk-eval-f's 4,513), so the entry is given as code
-- of the source term and its parts are held as calls
nk-entry-code : Code
nk-entry-code = code (λ (n x : Word) → nk-eval-f (nk-fuel-of n) (nk-term-of n x))
